☕ Java Basics Revision Roadmap
🟢 Phase 1 — Classes & Objects

Start here.

*Create a Student class with fields like name, age, marks.
*Create objects and print their data.
*Create a Car class and initialize multiple objects.
*Add methods like displayDetails().
*Create a Rectangle class with methods for area and perimeter.
*Create an Employee class and calculate annual salary.
*Create a Book class and display book information.
*Create a BankAccount class with deposit() and withdraw() methods.

Concepts:
class, object, fields, methods, object creation, instance variables.

🟢 Phase 2 — Constructors
Create a Student using a default constructor.
Create a Student using a parameterized constructor.
Create a Book with multiple constructors.
Demonstrate constructor overloading.
Create an Employee class using this.

Concepts:
constructors, this, constructor overloading.

🟢 Phase 3 — Methods
Method with no parameters/no return value.
Method with parameters/no return value.
Method with parameters/return value.
Method with no parameters/return value.
Create a calculator using methods.
Create methods to check:
even/odd
positive/negative
prime number
palindrome
factorial

Concepts:
parameters, return values, method calling, method overloading.

🟡 Phase 4 — Variables & Modifiers
Demonstrate local, instance, and static variables.
Create a Counter class using a static variable.
Create a program demonstrating static methods.
Use final variables.
Create a class with private fields and access them through methods.

Concepts:
static, final, access modifiers, scope.

🟡 Phase 5 — Encapsulation
Create a Student class with private fields.
Add getters and setters.
Validate marks before setting them.
Create a BankAccount with controlled deposit/withdrawal.
Create an Employee class where salary cannot be negative.

Concepts:
private, getters/setters, data hiding, validation.

🟡 Phase 6 — Inheritance
Animal → Dog
Vehicle → Car
Employee → Manager
Demonstrate single-level inheritance.
Demonstrate multilevel inheritance.
Demonstrate hierarchical inheritance.
Use super to access parent members.
Use super() to call a parent constructor.

Concepts:
extends, super, parent/child classes.

🟠 Phase 7 — Polymorphism
Method overloading calculator.
Method overriding using Animal → Dog/Cat.
Create a Shape class with overridden area().
Demonstrate upcasting.
Demonstrate runtime method dispatch.

Concepts:
overloading, overriding, upcasting, runtime polymorphism.

🟠 Phase 8 — Abstraction
Create an abstract Shape class.
Create Circle, Rectangle, Triangle.
Create an abstract Employee class.
Create an interface Payment.
Implement it using UPIPayment, CardPayment, CashPayment.
Demonstrate multiple interfaces.

Concepts:
abstract, abstract methods, interfaces, implements.

🔵 Phase 9 — Arrays & Strings
Find largest/smallest element in an array.
Calculate sum and average.
Reverse an array.
Sort an array.
Search for an element.
Find duplicate elements.
Count frequency of elements.
Reverse a String.
Check String palindrome.
Count vowels/consonants.
Count words.
Find duplicate characters.

Concepts:
arrays, String, StringBuilder, loops.

🔵 Phase 10 — Exception Handling
Handle division by zero.
Handle invalid array index.
Handle invalid number input.
Use try-catch-finally.
Use multiple catch blocks.
Create your own exception: InvalidAgeException.
Create a bank withdrawal exception.

Concepts:
try, catch, finally, throw, throws, custom exceptions.

🟣 Phase 11 — Collections

Then move to:

ArrayList — add/remove/search elements.
LinkedList.
HashSet — remove duplicates.
HashMap — student name → marks.
Iterate using enhanced for.
Iterate using Iterator.
Sort an ArrayList.
Find frequency using HashMap.

Concepts:
List, Set, Map, generics, iterators.

🟣 Phase 12 — File Handling
Write data to a file.
Read data from a file.
Append data.
Count lines/words in a file.
Store student records in a file.

Concepts:
File, FileReader, FileWriter, buffering, exceptions.
